<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>From vMF encoder to InfoNCE loss</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall the encoder defines a von Mises–Fisher (vMF) density on the unit
hypersphere:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}(z\mid s)=C_{d}(\kappa)\,\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s)^{\top}z\big),\quad\|z\|_{2}=\|\mu_{\phi}(s)\|_{2}=1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}(z\mid s)=C_{d}(\kappa)\,\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s)^{\top}z\big),\quad\|z\|_{2}=\|\mu_{\phi}(s)\|_{2}=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{d}(\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{d}(\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalizing constant and
<math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given an anchor <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{a}</annotation></semantics></math> and a candidate set <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=\{z^{+},z_{1}^{-},\ldots,z_{K}^{-}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=\{z^{+},z_{1}^{-},\ldots,z_{K}^{-}\}</annotation></semantics></math>
containing one positive and <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> negatives, consider the conditional probability that
the positive <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> was generated from <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{\phi}(\cdot\mid s^{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}(\cdot\mid s^{a})</annotation></semantics></math> among the candidates:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\phi}\!\left(\text{pos}=z^{+}\,\middle|\,s^{a},\mathcal{C}\right)=\frac{q_{\phi}(z^{+}\mid s^{a})}{\sum\limits_{z\in\mathcal{C}}q_{\phi}(z\mid s^{a})}=\frac{C_{d}(\kappa)\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})^{\top}z^{+}\big)}{\sum\limits_{z\in\mathcal{C}}C_{d}(\kappa)\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})^{\top}z\big)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtext>pos</mtext><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\phi}\!\left(\text{pos}=z^{+}\,\middle|\,s^{a},\mathcal{C}\right)=\frac{q_{\phi}(z^{+}\mid s^{a})}{\sum\limits_{z\in\mathcal{C}}q_{\phi}(z\mid s^{a})}=\frac{C_{d}(\kappa)\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})^{\top}z^{+}\big)}{\sum\limits_{z\in\mathcal{C}}C_{d}(\kappa)\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})^{\top}z\big)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed, <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{d}(\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{d}(\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> cancels:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\phi}\!\left(\text{pos}=z^{+}\,\middle|\,s^{a},\mathcal{C}\right)=\frac{\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})^{\top}z^{+}\big)}{\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})^{\top}z^{+}\big)+\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})^{\top}z_{j}^{-}\big)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtext>pos</mtext><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\phi}\!\left(\text{pos}=z^{+}\,\middle|\,s^{a},\mathcal{C}\right)=\frac{\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})^{\top}z^{+}\big)}{\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})^{\top}z^{+}\big)+\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})^{\top}z_{j}^{-}\big)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Maximizing the log-likelihood of the correct positive is therefore equivalent to minimizing
the cross-entropy loss</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{NCE}}=-\log\frac{\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})^{\top}z^{+}\big)}{\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})^{\top}z^{+}\big)+\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})^{\top}z_{j}^{-}\big)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>NCE</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{NCE}}=-\log\frac{\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})^{\top}z^{+}\big)}{\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})^{\top}z^{+}\big)+\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\!\big(\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})^{\top}z_{j}^{-}\big)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Identifying the <em id="A1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">similarity</em> as the dot product on the unit sphere,
<math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{sim}(u,v)=u^{\top}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>sim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{sim}(u,v)=u^{\top}v</annotation></semantics></math> (cosine similarity), and setting the temperature <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1/\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1/\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>,
we obtain the standard InfoNCE form:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{InfoNCE}}=-\log\frac{\exp\!\big(\mathrm{sim}(\mu_{\phi}(s^{a}),z^{+})/T\big)}{\exp\!\big(\mathrm{sim}(\mu_{\phi}(s^{a}),z^{+})/T\big)+\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\!\big(\mathrm{sim}(\mu_{\phi}(s^{a}),z_{j}^{-})/T\big)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>InfoNCE</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{InfoNCE}}=-\log\frac{\exp\!\big(\mathrm{sim}(\mu_{\phi}(s^{a}),z^{+})/T\big)}{\exp\!\big(\mathrm{sim}(\mu_{\phi}(s^{a}),z^{+})/T\big)+\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\!\big(\mathrm{sim}(\mu_{\phi}(s^{a}),z_{j}^{-})/T\big)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">If we instantiate the candidates by their mean directions, i.e.,
<math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{a}=\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{a}=\mu_{\phi}(s^{a})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{+}=\mu_{\phi}(s^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{+}=\mu_{\phi}(s^{+})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{j}^{-}=\mu_{\phi}(s_{j}^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{j}^{-}=\mu_{\phi}(s_{j}^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>,
then the loss reduces exactly to the
temperature-scaled dot-product InfoNCE used in the main text
(with <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1/\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1/\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Within–Motion Alignment</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We prove that under the InfoNCE objective with “same–motion” positives, the optimal encoder perfectly aligns all frames of a given motion to a single unit vector on the sphere.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let there be <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> motions. Each motion <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\{m_{1},\dots,m_{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\{m_{1},\dots,m_{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sequence of states <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. An encoder <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> maps each state to a unit vector <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=\mu_{\phi}(s)\in\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=\mu_{\phi}(s)\in\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For an anchor <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in m</annotation></semantics></math>, we draw a positive <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in m</annotation></semantics></math> (independent) and negatives <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{1},\dots,n_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{1},\dots,n_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> from other motions. The InfoNCE loss for this triplet is</p>
<table id="A2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(u,v,\{n_{j}\})\;=\;-\log\frac{\exp(u^{\top}v/T)}{\exp(u^{\top}v/T)+\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp(u^{\top}n_{j}/T)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(u,v,\{n_{j}\})\;=\;-\log\frac{\exp(u^{\top}v/T)}{\exp(u^{\top}v/T)+\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp(u^{\top}n_{j}/T)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and negatives <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{n_{j}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{n_{j}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Write <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=u^{\top}v\in[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=u^{\top}v\in[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\sum_{j}\exp(u^{\top}n_{j}/T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\sum_{j}\exp(u^{\top}n_{j}/T)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(s)\;=\;-\frac{s}{T}+\log\!\big(\exp(s/T)+C\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(s)\;=\;-\frac{s}{T}+\log\!\big(\exp(s/T)+C\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Differentiating LHS with <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d\ell}{ds}\;=\;\frac{1}{T}\Big(-\frac{C}{\exp(s/T)+C}\Big)\;&lt;\;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d\ell}{ds}\;=\;\frac{1}{T}\Big(-\frac{C}{\exp(s/T)+C}\Big)\;&lt;\;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">so <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(s)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> is monotonically decreasing in <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math></span>. Hence, the loss is minimized by maximizing <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\top}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\top}v</annotation></semantics></math>, which is at most <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and attained only when <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=u</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that the angle between embeddings of frames from the same motion should be minimized, resulting in a perfect alignment.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reduction of the loss.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After the alignment, for motion <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=v=\mu_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=v=\mu_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and equation <a href="#A2.E8" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Within–Motion Alignment ‣ Reference Grounded Skill Discovery" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> reduces to</p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{m}=-\log\frac{e^{1/T}}{e^{1/T}+\sum_{j\neq m}e^{\mu_{m}^{\top}\mu_{j}/T}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{m}=-\log\frac{e^{1/T}}{e^{1/T}+\sum_{j\neq m}e^{\mu_{m}^{\top}\mu_{j}/T}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The total loss <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{m}\ell_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>m</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{m}\ell_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> now depends only on the pairwise inner products <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{m}^{\top}\mu_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{m}^{\top}\mu_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Minimizing this objective pushes the vectors <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mu_{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mu_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math> as far apart as geometry allows, yielding a regular simplex when <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\leq k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\leq k+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of guarantee as an imitation reward</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our goal is to prove two properties of the reward function in Eq. <a href="#S4.E7" title="In 4.2 Imitation of reference skills ‣ 4 Reference Grounded Skill Discovery ‣ Reference Grounded Skill Discovery" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>:
<span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(i)</span> the reward achieves its optimum when the agent visits the exact states of motion <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<span id="A3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(ii)</span> the reward function is locally quasi-concave around the states <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in m</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Proof of reward optimality on motion states</h3>

<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Assumption.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We assume that the pretraining of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> in Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Pretraining: grounding latent space on reference motions ‣ 4 Reference Grounded Skill Discovery ‣ Reference Grounded Skill Discovery" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> has reached its theoretical optimum. More concretely, for all <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and for all <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{1},s_{2},\ldots,s_{l_{m}}\}\subset m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{1},s_{2},\ldots,s_{l_{m}}\}\subset m</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\phi}(s_{1})=\mu_{\phi}(s_{2})=\cdots=\mu_{\phi}(s_{l_{m}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\phi}(s_{1})=\mu_{\phi}(s_{2})=\cdots=\mu_{\phi}(s_{l_{m}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of states in motion <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, from Eq. <a href="#S4.E5" title="In 4.2 Imitation of reference skills ‣ 4 Reference Grounded Skill Discovery ‣ Reference Grounded Skill Discovery" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{m}=\frac{1}{l_{m}}\sum_{s\in m}\mu_{\phi}(s)=\frac{1}{l_{m}}\,l_{m}\,\mu_{\phi}(s_{i})=\mu_{\phi}(s_{i}),\quad\forall i." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{m}=\frac{1}{l_{m}}\sum_{s\in m}\mu_{\phi}(s)=\frac{1}{l_{m}}\,l_{m}\,\mu_{\phi}(s_{i})=\mu_{\phi}(s_{i}),\quad\forall i.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
From Eq. <a href="#S4.E7" title="In 4.2 Imitation of reference skills ‣ 4 Reference Grounded Skill Discovery ‣ Reference Grounded Skill Discovery" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, the reward can be written as</p>
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r(s,z_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r(s,z_{m})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log p(z)+\log q_{\phi}(z_{m}\mid s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log p(z)+\log q_{\phi}(z_{m}\mid s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C+\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s)^{\top}z_{m}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C+\kappa\,\mu_{\phi}(s)^{\top}z_{m},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> are constants that do not affect the optimal point. Discarding the constants, we can write</p>
<table id="A3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s,z_{m})=\langle\mu_{\phi}(s),z_{m}\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s,z_{m})=\langle\mu_{\phi}(s),z_{m}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\phi}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\phi}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> with Eq. <a href="#A3.E9" title="In Assumption. ‣ C.1 Proof of reward optimality on motion states ‣ Appendix C Proof of guarantee as an imitation reward ‣ Reference Grounded Skill Discovery" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall s\in m,\,r(s,z_{m})=\langle\mu_{\phi}(s),z_{m}\rangle=\langle z_{m},z_{m}\rangle=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall s\in m,\,r(s,z_{m})=\langle\mu_{\phi}(s),z_{m}\rangle=\langle z_{m},z_{m}\rangle=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s,z_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s,z_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded within <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, this value is the global optimum. Hence, every state <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in m</annotation></semantics></math> achieves the global optimum.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Proof of local quasi-concavity of the reward</h3>

<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Assumption.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We assume from Eq. <a href="#A3.E9" title="In Assumption. ‣ C.1 Proof of reward optimality on motion states ‣ Appendix C Proof of guarantee as an imitation reward ‣ Reference Grounded Skill Discovery" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> that for every <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\star}\in m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\star}\in m</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\phi}(s^{\star})=z_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\phi}(s^{\star})=z_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. We designed the neural network <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> to be piecewise linear in a neighborhood of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, and normalization is applied to the output so that <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\phi}(s)=\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s)/\|\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\phi}(s)=\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s)/\|\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s)\|</annotation></semantics></math> lies in a unit hypersphere for all <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Lemma.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\star}\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\star}\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> be a state in a motion that satisfies <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\phi}(s^{\star})=\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s^{\star})/\|\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s^{\star})\|_{2}=z_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\phi}(s^{\star})=\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s^{\star})/\|\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s^{\star})\|_{2}=z_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s):=\langle\mu_{\phi}(s),z_{m}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s):=\langle\mu_{\phi}(s),z_{m}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is quasi-concave in a neighborhood of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To show that <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s)</annotation></semantics></math> is quasi-concave in a neighborhood of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, we want to show that inside the neighborhood <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>, the superlevel set <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\alpha}(r)=\{s:r(s)\geq\alpha\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\alpha}(r)=\{s:r(s)\geq\alpha\}</annotation></semantics></math> is convex.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To show this, we first check the convexity of the superlevel set in the latent space.
Then, by leveraging the fact that the preimage of an affine transform preserves convexity, we conclude the convexity of the superlevel set in the state space.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Convexity of superlevel set in latent space.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define a function in latent space <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(z)=z_{m}^{\top}z/\|z\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(z)=z_{m}^{\top}z/\|z\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. This satisfies <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s))=r(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s))=r(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We now show the convexity of the superlevel set of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{\alpha}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{\alpha}(f)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{\,z:\ f(z)=z_{m}^{\top}\tfrac{z}{\|z\|_{2}}\geq\alpha\,\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{\,z:\ f(z)=z_{m}^{\top}\tfrac{z}{\|z\|_{2}}\geq\alpha\,\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{\,z:\ z_{m}^{\top}z\geq\alpha\|z\|_{2}\,\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{\,z:\ z_{m}^{\top}z\geq\alpha\|z\|_{2}\,\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To show its convexity, for <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall z_{1},z_{2}\in S_{\alpha}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall z_{1},z_{2}\in S_{\alpha}(f)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, we plug in <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\leftarrow tz_{1}+(1-t)z_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\leftarrow tz_{1}+(1-t)z_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle z_{m}^{\top}\!\big(tz_{1}+(1-t)z_{2}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle z_{m}^{\top}\!\big(tz_{1}+(1-t)z_{2}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=tz_{m}^{\top}z_{1}+(1-t)z_{m}^{\top}z_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=tz_{m}^{\top}z_{1}+(1-t)z_{m}^{\top}z_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq t\alpha\|z_{1}\|_{2}+(1-t)\alpha\|z_{2}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq t\alpha\|z_{1}\|_{2}+(1-t)\alpha\|z_{2}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\big(\|tz_{1}\|_{2}+\|(1-t)z_{2}\|_{2}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\big(\|tz_{1}\|_{2}+\|(1-t)z_{2}\|_{2}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\alpha\|tz_{1}+(1-t)z_{2}\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\alpha\|tz_{1}+(1-t)z_{2}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="tz_{1}+(1-t)z_{2}\in S_{\alpha}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">tz_{1}+(1-t)z_{2}\in S_{\alpha}(f)</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\alpha}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\alpha}(f)</annotation></semantics></math> is convex.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Convexity of superlevel set in state space.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we use the fact that the preimage of an affine transform also preserves convexity: when <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(s):=As+b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(s):=As+b</annotation></semantics></math> is affine, then <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{-1}(S_{\alpha}(f))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{-1}(S_{\alpha}(f))</annotation></semantics></math> is convex.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The superlevel set of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s)=f(\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s)=f(\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s))</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{\alpha}(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{\alpha}(r)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\big\{s:r(s)\geq\alpha\,\big\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\big\{s:r(s)\geq\alpha\,\big\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\big\{s:f(\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s))\geq\alpha\,\big\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\big\{s:f(\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s))\geq\alpha\,\big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Since the affine property only applies near the neighborhood of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can define an open ball around <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies such a condition:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s)\;=\;As+b\qquad\text{for all }s\in B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star}):=\{s:\ \|s-s^{\star}\|_{2}&lt;\epsilon\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s)\;=\;As+b\qquad\text{for all }s\in B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star}):=\{s:\ \|s-s^{\star}\|_{2}&lt;\epsilon\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Restricting the domain to the ball, we have:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\{s\in B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star}):r(s)\geq\alpha\,\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{s\in B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star}):r(s)\geq\alpha\,\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=S_{\alpha}(r)\cap B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=S_{\alpha}(r)\cap B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\big\{s:r(s)\geq\alpha\,\big\}\cap B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\big\{s:r(s)\geq\alpha\,\big\}\cap B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\big\{s:f(\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s))\geq\alpha\,\big\}\cap B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\big\{s:f(\hat{\mu}_{\phi}(s))\geq\alpha\,\big\}\cap B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\big\{s:f(T(s))\geq\alpha\,\big\}\cap B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\big\{s:f(T(s))\geq\alpha\,\big\}\cap B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=T^{-1}(\{z:f(z)\geq\alpha\})\cap B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=T^{-1}(\{z:f(z)\geq\alpha\})\cap B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=T^{-1}(S_{\alpha}(f))\cap B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=T^{-1}(S_{\alpha}(f))\cap B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This set is also convex because the intersection of two convex sets is also convex. This proves that the superlevel set of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is convex local to <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conclusion</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By definition of quasi-concavity, we conclude that <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is quasi-concave in the neighborhood of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\epsilon}(s^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Full algorithm of RGSD</h2>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> RGSD - Pretraining</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
           Initialize encoder function <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, reference dataset <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> to # of epochs <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
            Sample <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\sim\operatorname{Uniform}(\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\sim\operatorname{Uniform}(\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
            Sample <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{a},x^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{a},x^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="alg1.l4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{M}-m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{M}-m\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
            Update <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{InfoNCE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>InfoNCE</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{InfoNCE}}</annotation></semantics></math> on Eq. <a href="#S4.E4" title="In 4.1 Pretraining: grounding latent space on reference motions ‣ 4 Reference Grounded Skill Discovery ‣ Reference Grounded Skill Discovery" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After pretraining is completed, imitatino and discovery happen in parallel.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> RGSD: Imitation &amp; Discovery</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initialize:</span> skill-conditioned policy <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, frozen pretrained encoder <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{-}_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{-}_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, trainable encoder <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, imitation ratio <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, KL loss coefficient <math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, reference dataset <math id="alg2.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, set of reference motion embeddings <math id="alg2.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>, feature mask <math id="alg2.l1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\text{mask}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>mask</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\text{mask}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and replay buffer <math id="alg2.l1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
           Initialize <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}\leftarrow q^{-}_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}\leftarrow q^{-}_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> number of epochs <span id="alg2.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> episodes per epoch <span id="alg2.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
             Sample task indicator <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\sim\operatorname{Bernoulli}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Bernoulli</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\sim\operatorname{Bernoulli}(p)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l5.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><span id="alg2.l5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// 1 being imitation, 0 being discovery</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
             Sample reference <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\sim\operatorname{Uniform}(\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\sim\operatorname{Uniform}(\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
             Initialize <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\sim\operatorname{Uniform}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\sim\operatorname{Uniform}(m)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
             Compute <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S4.E5" title="In 4.2 Imitation of reference skills ‣ 4 Reference Grounded Skill Discovery ‣ Reference Grounded Skill Discovery" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> with <math id="alg2.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{-}_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{-}_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\leftarrow z_{m}\cdot c+k/\|k\|\cdot(1-c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\leftarrow z_{m}\cdot c+k/\|k\|\cdot(1-c)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="alg2.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
             
</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg2.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> episode not done <span id="alg2.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
              Execute <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s,z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s,z)</annotation></semantics></math>, observe <math id="alg2.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
              Compute reward <math id="alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leftarrow\text{Const.}+\log q^{-}_{\phi}(z\mid s^{\prime})\cdot c+\log q_{\phi}(z\mid s^{\prime})\cdot(1-c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>Const.</mtext><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leftarrow\text{Const.}+\log q^{-}_{\phi}(z\mid s^{\prime})\cdot c+\log q_{\phi}(z\mid s^{\prime})\cdot(1-c)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
              Add <math id="alg2.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s,a,r,s^{\prime},z,c\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s,a,r,s^{\prime},z,c\}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            
              <math id="alg2.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leftarrow s^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leftarrow s^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg2.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each <math id="alg2.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s,a,r,s^{\prime},z,c\}\in\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s,a,r,s^{\prime},z,c\}\in\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
            
            
             Compute <math id="alg2.l19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\phi}\leftarrow(1-c)\cdot(-\log q_{\phi}(z\mid s^{\prime}))+\alpha*c\cdot\operatorname{KL}\!\big(q_{\phi}(\cdot|s)\,\|\,q^{-}_{\phi}(\cdot|s)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\phi}\leftarrow(1-c)\cdot(-\log q_{\phi}(z\mid s^{\prime}))+\alpha*c\cdot\operatorname{KL}\!\big(q_{\phi}(\cdot|s)\,\|\,q^{-}_{\phi}(\cdot|s)\big)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
            
            
             Update <math id="alg2.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> to minimize <math id="alg2.l20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
            
            
             Update <math id="alg2.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> using PPO with rewards <math id="alg2.l21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">22:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">23:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l23.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Experiments details</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>State and Action space</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a 3D SMPL humanoid character, commonly adopted in prior work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luo et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tessler et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tirinzoni et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. The state representation is defined as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">phase variable: <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-D</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">root (pelvis) height - <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-D</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">root rotation relative to the local coordinate frame, <math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="69" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>69</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">69</annotation></semantics></math>-D</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">local rotation of each joint, , <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="144" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>144</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">144</annotation></semantics></math>-D</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">local velocity of each joint, and , <math id="A5.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="72" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>72</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">72</annotation></semantics></math>-D</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">positions of the hands and feet in the local coordinate frame. <math id="A5.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="72" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>72</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">72</annotation></semantics></math>D</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">While policy and value function takes single frame observation as input, encoder takes 5 frames concatenated the latest 5 steps of observations as input, <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}=(o_{t-4},o_{t-3},o_{t-2},o_{t-1},o_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}=(o_{t-4},o_{t-3},o_{t-2},o_{t-1},o_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The agent controls the character by outputting target rotations for PD controllers at each joint. In total the character has 23 spherical joints, resulting in 69D action space.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Implementation Details of Baseline algorithms</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To isolate the algorithmic contributions, we removed all additional engineering techniques applied in the original implementations to improve motion robustness.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For <span id="A5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ASE</span>, the original training introduces recovery strategies by initializing <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\%</annotation></semantics></math> of the environments in random fallen states. While this clearly improves robustness, we removed this component consistently across our method and all baselines. ASE also incorporates an auxiliary diversity objective:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{\mathrm{div}}=\mathbb{E}_{d^{\pi}(s)}\;\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},z_{2}\sim p(z)}\left[\left(\frac{D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(\pi(\cdot\mid s,z_{1}),\;\pi(\cdot\mid s,z_{2})\right)}{D_{Z}(z_{1},z_{2})}-1\right)^{2}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>div</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{\mathrm{div}}=\mathbb{E}_{d^{\pi}(s)}\;\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},z_{2}\sim p(z)}\left[\left(\frac{D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(\pi(\cdot\mid s,z_{1}),\;\pi(\cdot\mid s,z_{2})\right)}{D_{Z}(z_{1},z_{2})}-1\right)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> is a distance function. Together with the mutual information objective, <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{\mathrm{div}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>div</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{\mathrm{div}}</annotation></semantics></math> encourages policies to exhibit diverse behaviors when conditioned on different latent variables. Although this objective is modular and could be applied to any baseline, we excluded it to focus strictly on the main algorithmic differences.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For <span id="A5.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CALM</span>, we encoded entire motions rather than segmenting them into <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-second clips, since the motion lengths we used (between <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> seconds) are relatively short. Shorter motions were zero-padded to standardize sequence lengths.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, following conventions in skill discovery frameworks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gregor et al., 2016</a>; <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Eysenbach et al., 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Laskin et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Park et al., 2023b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rho et al., </a>)</cite>, we sampled a skill latent at the beginning of each episode and kept it fixed throughout the rollout. While transitioning between skills is orthogonal and can be incorporated into both our method and the baselines to further improve robustness, we excluded it here to focus on a clean understanding of algorithmic contributions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>List of reference motions</h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We list the file names (relative paths) of all motions used in our experiments:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
